---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Economy · Meridian"
  description="A live read on the Meridian server economy: the Meridian Economic Index, money supply, trade volume, and prices."
  path="/economy"
  analytics
>
<main class="doc">
  <h1>Economy</h1>
  <p class="lead"></p>
  <div class="data-stale" data-stale hidden></div>

  <div class="analytics" data-analytics>
    <!-- Ordered the way an economic report is ordered: the rules of the
         economy first, then money, prices, activity and distribution. Each
         figure appears exactly once, with the chart it belongs to. -->
    <section id="flow">
      <h2>How money works</h2>
      <p>The currency of this server is Gold (G). A gold ingot is 1 G and a gold block is 9 G, and the items themselves are the money: there is no balance anywhere else. Gold can be obtained through mining, voting, or trading with players. There is no server shop.</p>
      <p>Gold is used to purchase land claims, pay upkeep, establish nations, and for various other expenses.</p>
      <p>Personal banks do not exist. Gold can only be stored in chests and land banks. Because the money is physical, the figures below are counted from the world itself rather than from a ledger.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="money">
      <h2>Money</h2>
      <div class="stat-row" data-slot="stat-money"></div>
      <div class="chart">
        <h3>Gold supply</h3>
        <div class="c-sub">Every gold ingot and block in the world, counted from player inventories, ender chests, containers, and land banks. Gold in a land bank has left circulation until it is withdrawn.</div>
        <div data-slot="supply-chart"></div>
        <div class="c-sub" data-slot="coverage"></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="prices">
      <h2>Prices</h2>
      <div class="stat-row" data-slot="stat-prices"></div>
      <div class="chart">
        <h3>Price index</h3>
        <div data-slot="price-chart"></div>
      </div>
      <div data-slot="item-table"></div>
      <h3>Daily range</h3>
      <div class="candles" data-slot="candles"></div>
    </section>

    <section id="trade">
      <h2>Trade</h2>
      <div class="stat-row" data-slot="stat-trade"></div>
      <div class="chart">
        <h3>Shop trade</h3>
        <div class="c-sub">Gold paid through player chest shops each day.</div>
        <div data-slot="volume-chart"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="chart">
        <h3>Gold spent</h3>
        <div class="c-sub">All gold leaving player hands each day: shop purchases, claim costs, upkeep, deposits, and payments.</div>
        <div data-slot="flow-chart"></div>
      </div>
    </section>

  </div>
</main>
</Base>
